1
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:49,382
<i>There's a reason you're still alive.</i>

2
00:00:49,466 --> 00:00:50,925
What are you saying?

3
00:00:51,009 --> 00:00:55,013
For 20 years, I prepared
for this very moment.

4
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:57,974
How could you be so sure
that this day would come?

5
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,601
<i>That I'd still keep our promise?</i>

6
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:01,144
<i>Our plans.</i>

7
00:01:01,227 --> 00:01:04,606
I was slowly preparing this
for your return.

8
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:09,903
<i>Don't waste your pain.</i>

9
00:01:09,986 --> 00:01:12,322
<i>Make it your reason to fight.</i>

10
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:15,784
Let's help each other.
While you seek justice,

11
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:17,702
I will help you live your life again.

12
00:01:19,704 --> 00:01:22,916
If someone is making a move
around Mikoy and Chiara,

13
00:01:22,999 --> 00:01:24,250
we can't rule out

14
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:26,795
that they're connected to La Concordat.

15
00:01:32,383 --> 00:01:34,677
We don't know yet. No assumptions.

16
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:35,595
We need facts.

17
00:01:38,598 --> 00:01:42,060
Mario. Some information
came in at the agency.

18
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:42,977
It's not verified yet.

19
00:01:43,061 --> 00:01:45,939
<i>So I can't give you the details.</i>

20
00:01:46,523 --> 00:01:48,441
Keep an eye on your surroundings for now.

21
00:01:48,525 --> 00:01:50,110
I'll handle things here.

22
00:01:52,112 --> 00:01:53,822
- Mario!
- Mario!

23
00:01:53,905 --> 00:01:54,864
Mario, there's a fire!

24
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:56,366
Come on, let's go!

25
00:01:57,033 --> 00:01:58,201
Hurry up!

26
00:01:58,284 --> 00:02:00,411
- Faster!
- Sir Mario.

27
00:02:00,495 --> 00:02:01,329
Where?

28
00:02:01,412 --> 00:02:03,498
- Over there!
- Hurry!

29
00:02:03,581 --> 00:02:04,833
Let's get out!

30
00:02:04,916 --> 00:02:06,251
- Bags.
- Quick!

31
00:02:06,334 --> 00:02:07,961
- What's the update?
- Mar.

32
00:02:08,044 --> 00:02:10,672
Looks like the portable fan overheated.

33
00:02:10,755 --> 00:02:12,549
Good thing we noticed it right away,

34
00:02:12,632 --> 00:02:14,092
so the fire didn't spread.

35
00:02:14,676 --> 00:02:16,261
It was pretty close to our house, too.

36
00:02:16,344 --> 00:02:17,929
My buzz is gone.

37
00:02:18,012 --> 00:02:20,098
I got really scared, Mario.

38
00:02:20,181 --> 00:02:22,183
Thank God no one got hurt, right?

39
00:02:22,267 --> 00:02:23,309
Exactly.

40
00:02:24,018 --> 00:02:25,103
Okay, Mar.

41
00:02:25,812 --> 00:02:26,938
We'll double-check the area first.

42
00:02:27,021 --> 00:02:27,856
Okay, okay. Thanks.

43
00:02:30,275 --> 00:02:31,151
Come out!

44
00:02:31,234 --> 00:02:32,318
Hurry.

45
00:02:34,737 --> 00:02:35,655
Mario.

46
00:02:36,239 --> 00:02:38,408
Good thing it was just a small fire.

47
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:40,410
I thought there was another Manananggal.

48
00:02:42,162 --> 00:02:44,164
But this isn't an isolated incident.

49
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:47,250
Especially now that
there's someone lurking around,

50
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:50,003
that vigilante you call a Manananggal.

51
00:02:50,837 --> 00:02:52,630
But we've been through this before.

52
00:02:53,131 --> 00:02:54,173
In Cebu.

53
00:02:54,257 --> 00:02:57,635
Remember how it started small,
then got worse over time?

54
00:02:58,303 --> 00:03:00,638
But, Captain Pepe, maybe tomorrow,

55
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:03,057
you can start patrolling again.

56
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:05,310
Not because we're panicking.

57
00:03:05,393 --> 00:03:07,604
We just want to make sure we're safe.

58
00:03:08,187 --> 00:03:10,273
- Yes, Mario.
- We're game!

59
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:15,236
Wait, one more thing.

60
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:17,155
As much as possible,

61
00:03:17,238 --> 00:03:19,991
don't tell anyone about this. Not a soul.

62
00:03:20,074 --> 00:03:21,743
Especially Chiara and Mikoy.

63
00:03:22,785 --> 00:03:23,995
They already have enough on their plate.

64
00:03:24,078 --> 00:03:25,747
We don't need to add to it.

65
00:03:25,830 --> 00:03:29,000
- You heard what Mario said.
- These two are such gossips.

66
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:31,044
Yes, sir. Yes, Mario.

67
00:03:31,127 --> 00:03:32,295
Yes? You two gossips?

68
00:03:32,378 --> 00:03:34,130
- No, sir.
- We're just drunk.

69
00:03:37,383 --> 00:03:38,843
Oh, gosh.

70
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:02,742
Here's your water bottle, sweetheart.

71
00:04:02,825 --> 00:04:04,869
I didn't wake you up early

72
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:06,204
because I thought,

73
00:04:06,287 --> 00:04:09,040
of course, my future wife
needs her beauty rest.

74
00:04:09,123 --> 00:04:11,125
We wouldn't want her
turning into a beast, right?

75
00:04:17,131 --> 00:04:19,676
My sweetheart is so sweet. He even got me

76
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:22,887
a tumbler.

77
00:04:22,971 --> 00:04:24,806
You remind me of someone

78
00:04:25,431 --> 00:04:26,683
I used to date

79
00:04:27,767 --> 00:04:29,269
- in Hong Kong.
- Huh?

80
00:04:29,978 --> 00:04:31,437
Dasho.

81
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:42,573
You know, I know him too.

82
00:04:43,199 --> 00:04:45,785
I know he's handsome and quite the catch,

83
00:04:45,868 --> 00:04:46,911
that Dasho.

84
00:04:47,662 --> 00:04:50,540
Yes, he's kind of like Mr. Suave.

85
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:54,502
Thank you, sweetheart,

86
00:04:55,837 --> 00:04:59,215
for taking care of me and for everything.

87
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:05,471
There you go.

88
00:05:06,347 --> 00:05:07,849
Why are you being so sweet today,
sweetheart?

89
00:05:07,932 --> 00:05:08,975
What's the occasion?

90
00:05:09,892 --> 00:05:11,436
You want something again, don't you?

91
00:05:12,687 --> 00:05:14,397
What could my sweetheart possibly want?

92
00:05:17,775 --> 00:05:19,902
- You idiot!
- Why?

93
00:05:20,486 --> 00:05:21,821
I'm just kidding.

94
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:28,244
I was just thinking.

95
00:05:33,207 --> 00:05:35,626
What if we don't go through
with the wedding?

96
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:50,224
Dara.

97
00:05:50,308 --> 00:05:51,434
Dara!

98
00:05:52,852 --> 00:05:54,187
Look.

99
00:05:54,270 --> 00:05:58,191
Sean looked like such an idiot.
He was so drunk at the bridal shower.

100
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:02,320
Carlota, I was there. I saw it in person.

101
00:06:03,946 --> 00:06:05,114
Were you there?

102
00:06:05,698 --> 00:06:08,618
Yes. You're just so whipped.

103
00:06:08,701 --> 00:06:12,330
You don't notice anything else
except that Sianong.

104
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:14,832
Well,

105
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:18,211
if by whipped, you mean head over heels,

106
00:06:19,212 --> 00:06:20,838
then yes.

107
00:06:20,922 --> 00:06:24,634
I'm head over heels in love with him.

108
00:06:24,717 --> 00:06:25,885
Anyway,

109
00:06:25,968 --> 00:06:28,054
look at this. Here.

110
00:06:28,137 --> 00:06:29,472
This is my favorite!

111
00:06:30,473 --> 00:06:32,433
There! Look.

112
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:38,022
Why do you look like you didn't sleep?

113
00:06:39,023 --> 00:06:39,941
I didn't.

114
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:42,777
Sean kept me up all night.

115
00:06:47,156 --> 00:06:51,035
Wait, wait. What does TMI mean?

116
00:06:51,119 --> 00:06:52,662
I don't want to talk about it.

117
00:06:52,745 --> 00:06:53,913
I don't want to talk about it.

118
00:06:56,791 --> 00:06:59,335
That's not what it means.

119
00:06:59,418 --> 00:07:00,294
No.

120
00:07:00,962 --> 00:07:03,506
I mean, I have some intel.

121
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:12,390
I mean, we're still getting married.

122
00:07:16,936 --> 00:07:19,063
It'll be simpler, more intimate.

123
00:07:19,147 --> 00:07:21,691
Fewer…

124
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:25,027
Fewer what?

125
00:07:27,488 --> 00:07:30,533
Fewer preparations.

126
00:07:30,616 --> 00:07:31,868
Right?

127
00:07:31,951 --> 00:07:33,494
It'll be cheaper, too.

128
00:07:33,578 --> 00:07:34,495
Think about it.

129
00:07:37,498 --> 00:07:38,499
Come here.

130
00:07:40,376 --> 00:07:41,502
Look at me.

131
00:07:46,382 --> 00:07:48,092
We're going through with the wedding.

132
00:07:49,844 --> 00:07:51,471
We're having the church wedding,

133
00:07:51,554 --> 00:07:53,431
we're having the reception,

134
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:57,143
and yes, we're doing
our dance numbers, too. Okay?

135
00:07:59,437 --> 00:08:01,731
I know you want everything to be simple,

136
00:08:02,523 --> 00:08:05,735
but I also know that's not
really the reason.

137
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:12,867
I know you're worried that your mom
and dad won't be able to make it.

138
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:17,038
I'm worried about that too, sweetheart.

139
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:20,082
Of course, I'm sad
that they won't be there, too.

140
00:08:21,626 --> 00:08:23,878
Because I want them to see you
walk down the aisle.

141
00:08:25,588 --> 00:08:27,548
I want them to see your smile

142
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:30,301
as you walk toward the altar.

143
00:08:31,135 --> 00:08:31,969
Right?

144
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:38,267
And of course, I want to hear
your dad say,

145
00:08:47,652 --> 00:08:49,570
just because they're not here

146
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:51,989
doesn't mean we shouldn't have a wedding.

147
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:56,035
If anything, I think we should
go through with it even more.

148
00:08:56,118 --> 00:08:57,453
Yes.

149
00:08:57,537 --> 00:08:59,205
So that someday,

150
00:08:59,288 --> 00:09:01,958
when we're finally reunited with them,

151
00:09:02,583 --> 00:09:04,210
we can be proud that

152
00:09:04,293 --> 00:09:08,172
we still made their dream come true,
of a happy life for you.

153
00:09:10,007 --> 00:09:10,967
Right?

154
00:09:12,176 --> 00:09:13,261
And one more thing, sweetheart.

155
00:09:13,344 --> 00:09:16,097
So many people helped us get this far.

156
00:09:17,098 --> 00:09:18,391
This wedding

157
00:09:18,474 --> 00:09:20,643
isn't just a celebration
for the two of us.

158
00:09:20,726 --> 00:09:23,062
It's also our way of saying thank you

159
00:09:23,145 --> 00:09:25,690
to everyone who loved us
and helped us along the way.

160
00:09:29,026 --> 00:09:30,653
Oh, and sweetheart,

161
00:09:30,736 --> 00:09:33,114
we've already paid our suppliers so much.

162
00:09:33,197 --> 00:09:34,240
What a waste!

163
00:09:34,323 --> 00:09:35,533
Oh my!

164
00:09:35,616 --> 00:09:37,201
I thought you were being serious.

165
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:38,619
I am serious, sweetheart.

166
00:09:39,203 --> 00:09:42,164
I'm just being practical, right?

167
00:09:44,208 --> 00:09:45,293
But wait.

168
00:09:45,793 --> 00:09:46,919
Why?

169
00:09:48,754 --> 00:09:52,550
Did you get a last-minute love confession?

170
00:09:52,633 --> 00:09:54,343
Is someone trying to steal you away?

171
00:09:54,427 --> 00:09:57,179
Hey! If there is, let them come out.

172
00:09:57,722 --> 00:09:59,223
- What?
- Sweetheart.

173
00:09:59,307 --> 00:10:00,808
They can all keep quiet forever.

174
00:10:02,351 --> 00:10:03,894
You guys are something else.

175
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:15,531
Did you hear about what happened
to Ma'am's husband?

176
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:17,366
The one who used to be here?

177
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:19,827
The bald guy, Viktor Valtrovi?

178
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:22,580
Yes. Apparently, he got badly beaten up.

179
00:10:22,663 --> 00:10:24,749
They even had to take him
to the clinic last night.

180
00:10:24,832 --> 00:10:26,417
What happened? Was there a riot?

181
00:10:27,501 --> 00:10:29,086
It's still unclear.

182
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:31,464
All they said was he could barely stand.

183
00:10:31,547 --> 00:10:34,008
I think we made the wrong call
letting him stay here.

184
00:10:34,091 --> 00:10:35,468
HQ is going to come after us for this.

185
00:10:35,551 --> 00:10:37,261
General Norberto might find out.

186
00:10:37,845 --> 00:10:38,679
Let's go.

187
00:10:50,107 --> 00:10:53,027
Word is Viktor underwent a medical exam.

188
00:10:54,612 --> 00:10:55,988
Why?

189
00:10:59,033 --> 00:11:01,077
Because of the severity of his injuries.

190
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:02,328
Injuries?

191
00:11:04,205 --> 00:11:05,373
How is he?

192
00:11:06,957 --> 00:11:07,958
It's still unclear.

193
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:11,379
There's no conclusive report yet.

194
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:17,676
We still don't know if there was a fight
or if he committed some violation inside.

195
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:21,514
Hold on.

196
00:11:21,597 --> 00:11:25,684
Carlota, why do you seem
so concerned about Viktor?

197
00:11:25,768 --> 00:11:29,897
Wasn't he the one
who wanted to have you killed?

198
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:32,024
Yes.

199
00:11:33,275 --> 00:11:37,113
But that doesn't mean
we both have to be bad people.

200
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:39,031
Besides,

201
00:11:42,368 --> 00:11:43,494
But

202
00:11:44,161 --> 00:11:46,288
I feel even worse for Chiara.

203
00:11:47,289 --> 00:11:48,999
You're worried about Chiara too?

204
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:50,543
I thought you two weren't on good terms.

205
00:11:52,002 --> 00:11:53,129
That was before.

206
00:11:53,838 --> 00:11:56,298
But she's different now.

207
00:11:59,969 --> 00:12:03,722
And she's no longer
the hot-headed assassin she used to be.

208
00:12:04,306 --> 00:12:06,809
Carlota, do you have a fever?

209
00:12:07,476 --> 00:12:10,438
You're worried about two people
who wanted to kill you?

210
00:12:19,238 --> 00:12:22,324
Maybe we can talk to General Norberto?

211
00:12:27,538 --> 00:12:28,747
There's an update.

212
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:33,169
No special permit.

213
00:12:35,045 --> 00:12:38,382
Viktor and Donabel won't be able
to attend the wedding.

214
00:12:48,893 --> 00:12:51,312
Chiara, Mikoy, dinner's ready!

215
00:12:51,395 --> 00:12:53,189
Come out already!

216
00:12:53,689 --> 00:12:56,150
- Hey, Vicky, I have a question for you.
- Go ahead.

217
00:12:56,233 --> 00:12:58,861
Are Italian men sweet?

218
00:12:59,445 --> 00:13:01,697
- At first.
- But?

219
00:13:02,364 --> 00:13:04,950
Once football comes into the picture,

220
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:06,660
you won't have a husband anymore.

221
00:13:10,331 --> 00:13:12,708
Well, I never married an Italian.

222
00:13:12,791 --> 00:13:14,627
I just heard those stories

223
00:13:14,710 --> 00:13:17,880
from my friends and colleagues
who married Italians.

224
00:13:17,963 --> 00:13:19,757
That's where I heard them.

225
00:13:20,841 --> 00:13:22,176
Okay, one more question.

226
00:13:22,259 --> 00:13:23,928
If you had to choose,

227
00:13:27,598 --> 00:13:28,474
Depends.

228
00:13:29,475 --> 00:13:30,476
On what?

229
00:13:30,559 --> 00:13:33,729
On who knows how to wash the dishes.

230
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:37,191
Good answer! You know my Mario?

231
00:13:37,274 --> 00:13:40,069
I was the one who taught him. Yes.

232
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:42,404
So, Mikoy,

233
00:13:42,488 --> 00:13:44,990
do you know how to wash the dishes?

234
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:47,993
Oh, really! Me? Of course I do!

235
00:13:48,077 --> 00:13:49,662
I know how to wash the dishes,

236
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:52,122
iron, sweep, and do the laundry.

237
00:13:52,206 --> 00:13:55,668
I even know how to bake.
I can do a somersault and shake my hips.

238
00:13:55,751 --> 00:13:58,629
Wow! Well, well, well.

239
00:13:58,712 --> 00:14:02,132
My girl really is lucky to have you!

240
00:14:02,216 --> 00:14:04,343
Oh, very lucky, Mama Vicky.

241
00:14:04,426 --> 00:14:06,720
I've truly been blessed with him.

242
00:14:09,056 --> 00:14:11,809
You two became such close friends
so quickly!

243
00:14:12,434 --> 00:14:14,186
Tell me about it!

244
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:15,271
You know, I feel like

245
00:14:15,354 --> 00:14:18,065
we've been friends for so long already.

246
00:14:18,148 --> 00:14:20,317
Right? And because of that,

247
00:14:21,193 --> 00:14:22,945
I have an idea, kids.

248
00:14:24,405 --> 00:14:28,701
Because, your Ninang Mylene won't be able
to make it to your wedding

249
00:14:28,784 --> 00:14:30,160
because of a family emergency…

250
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:35,457
It's such a shame, yes,
but I guess it's a blessing in disguise.

251
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:36,667
Why?

252
00:14:38,002 --> 00:14:43,716
Because Vicky has agreed to be
your wedding godmother.

253
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:44,884
Yes!

254
00:14:46,051 --> 00:14:47,469
- Really?
- Yes!

255
00:14:50,055 --> 00:14:51,056
Thank you so much!

256
00:14:53,934 --> 00:14:54,810
Mommy Vicky.

257
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:57,354
I'm just a little embarrassed because

258
00:14:57,438 --> 00:14:59,815
we don't really know each other
that well yet.

259
00:15:00,482 --> 00:15:01,817
For now.

260
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:05,070
Don't worry. We'll get
to know each other better.

261
00:15:05,154 --> 00:15:07,448
I still have plenty of time
to keep an eye on you

262
00:15:07,531 --> 00:15:11,452
and see if you're really perfect
for my girl.

263
00:15:11,535 --> 00:15:13,746
Yes, ma'am.

264
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:16,332
Behave yourself, Mikoy.

265
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:18,918
Let's eat.

266
00:15:20,169 --> 00:15:21,045
Let's eat.

267
00:15:24,006 --> 00:15:25,257
This smells good.

268
00:15:27,426 --> 00:15:28,427
So sweet!

269
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:41,774
I thought you were the bride.

270
00:15:42,608 --> 00:15:44,151
Why are you sneaking away?

271
00:15:45,277 --> 00:15:46,862
I am the bride,

272
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:48,447
not a hostage.

273
00:15:52,326 --> 00:15:53,786
How are they?

274
00:15:54,578 --> 00:15:55,537
Well…

275
00:15:56,372 --> 00:15:57,831
Last I heard,

276
00:15:58,582 --> 00:16:00,584
your mom is still as stubborn as ever,

277
00:16:01,168 --> 00:16:03,337
and your dad is even more stubborn.

278
00:16:08,842 --> 00:16:12,012
It's scarier when Dad is nice.

279
00:16:12,596 --> 00:16:15,099
It's even scarier when you're nice to me.

280
00:16:19,603 --> 00:16:23,399
Well, there's been
a little character development.

281
00:16:23,482 --> 00:16:27,152
The former hot-headed brat I knew

282
00:16:27,236 --> 00:16:32,533
is now a slightly less
hot-headed country girl.

283
00:16:34,451 --> 00:16:37,579
Well, it's easier to breathe in
the fresh air here.

284
00:16:37,663 --> 00:16:43,711
And it's refreshing to have
clean and clear life intentions.

285
00:16:45,546 --> 00:16:46,380
What?

286
00:16:47,089 --> 00:16:48,340
Are you ready?

287
00:16:53,721 --> 00:16:54,763
I'm ready.

288
00:16:58,058 --> 00:16:59,059
I just hope…

289
00:17:01,103 --> 00:17:04,857
Let's hope Viktor and Donabel can make it.

290
00:17:11,071 --> 00:17:12,531
Besides,

291
00:17:12,614 --> 00:17:15,242
it would be a shame
if they couldn't make it, right?

292
00:17:15,909 --> 00:17:17,536
You're their only daughter, after all.

293
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:24,418
It would be perfect if they could make it.

294
00:17:25,002 --> 00:17:26,253
You know what?

295
00:17:26,336 --> 00:17:28,380
Let's manifest it.

296
00:17:33,802 --> 00:17:35,262
Wait a minute.

297
00:17:35,345 --> 00:17:38,682
I thought our relationship
was leveling up.

298
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:40,017
Why am I still a Chihuahua?

299
00:17:52,237 --> 00:17:54,156
Come on. Let's go inside.

300
00:17:54,239 --> 00:17:55,908
They're waiting for you.

301
00:18:03,415 --> 00:18:06,085
Hey, what are you doing?

302
00:18:06,168 --> 00:18:07,544
You look like you're deep in thought.

303
00:18:07,628 --> 00:18:09,630
You've been stirring
that coffee for three hours.

304
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:12,508
Cocoy.

305
00:18:14,134 --> 00:18:16,261
What if we help Viktor?

306
00:18:17,054 --> 00:18:18,722
How do we help Viktor?

307
00:18:20,432 --> 00:18:21,266
We break him out.

308
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:23,477
What?

309
00:18:25,187 --> 00:18:26,438
It will be quick.

310
00:18:27,064 --> 00:18:28,607
We'll just get him out,

311
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:31,527
then bring him back after the wedding.

312
00:18:32,361 --> 00:18:34,154
Like we're just borrowing him.

313
00:18:35,781 --> 00:18:37,241
Come on, Carlota.

314
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:43,705
Viktor is a person, not something
that you can return after borrowing.

315
00:18:45,165 --> 00:18:46,166
Then,

316
00:18:50,337 --> 00:18:51,255
Look.

317
00:18:51,338 --> 00:18:53,966
Do you really think
that if Viktor escapes,

318
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:55,717
he'll come back?

319
00:18:58,053 --> 00:18:59,429
I'm just worried.

320
00:19:00,639 --> 00:19:01,557
Something's wrong.

321
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:30,544
But I have a crush on you.

322
00:19:31,712 --> 00:19:33,255
I have a crush on you too.

323
00:19:33,338 --> 00:19:35,132
So we're crushiecakes now?

324
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:42,222
Is it still replaying in your head?

325
00:19:45,642 --> 00:19:46,727
Alex.

326
00:19:47,477 --> 00:19:48,770
Is it that obvious?

327
00:19:49,813 --> 00:19:50,856
Very.

328
00:19:53,233 --> 00:19:56,528
Can't we just erase
whatever happened that night?

329
00:19:57,279 --> 00:19:59,448
We can't. It's already written.

330
00:20:01,533 --> 00:20:03,285
You know, Alex, you know how

331
00:20:03,368 --> 00:20:05,829
I confessed while I was drunk,

332
00:20:05,913 --> 00:20:08,040
and then we even got married?

333
00:20:08,749 --> 00:20:11,210
Doesn't that make me seem so easy?

334
00:20:12,252 --> 00:20:13,295
It's embarrassing.

335
00:20:14,671 --> 00:20:17,257
Now that you've finally said
how you really feel,

336
00:20:18,634 --> 00:20:21,053
I mean, you're free now.

337
00:20:21,136 --> 00:20:22,137
You've already won.

338
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:23,722
Not because you'll end up together.

339
00:20:23,805 --> 00:20:25,515
You've won because

340
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:28,310
you're no longer lying
about how you really feel.

341
00:20:28,393 --> 00:20:31,063
And you don't have anything
to hide anymore.

342
00:20:31,772 --> 00:20:33,023
That's true.

343
00:20:33,106 --> 00:20:35,859
It's just really hard
to repress your feelings.

344
00:20:35,943 --> 00:20:38,612
You know, it's kind of constipating?

345
00:20:39,404 --> 00:20:40,572
Isn't that true?

346
00:20:40,656 --> 00:20:42,366
Oh, Sofie.

347
00:20:43,242 --> 00:20:44,826
Right, Alex?

348
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:45,869
Do you get what I mean?

349
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:50,958
Well, if those hidden feelings
are stressing you out,

350
00:20:51,708 --> 00:20:53,043
then yes,

351
00:20:53,126 --> 00:20:54,753
it can affect your gut health.

352
00:20:55,587 --> 00:20:58,548
But if you both feel the same way,

353
00:20:58,632 --> 00:20:59,716
then that's good.

354
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:02,177
I think you'll be fine.

355
00:21:02,803 --> 00:21:04,638
You even got married, right?

356
00:21:08,141 --> 00:21:10,352
But wasn't he drunk too?

357
00:21:12,604 --> 00:21:14,481
Well, if he wasn't,

358
00:21:14,564 --> 00:21:16,650
at least you're free to move forward now.

359
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:20,904
You're right.

360
00:21:21,697 --> 00:21:22,531
You're right.

361
00:21:23,115 --> 00:21:24,783
I've said what I needed to say.

362
00:21:24,866 --> 00:21:26,702
Now, it's up to him.

363
00:21:45,929 --> 00:21:47,014
Chiara.

364
00:21:47,097 --> 00:21:48,348
Are you okay?

365
00:21:49,016 --> 00:21:51,101
Yes, Mom. I'm okay.

366
00:21:52,269 --> 00:21:56,815
I thought you were upset because I made
Vicky your wedding godmother.

367
00:21:58,191 --> 00:21:59,651
No, Mom.

368
00:22:01,028 --> 00:22:04,156
I was just surprised,
but of course, I'm happy because

369
00:22:04,239 --> 00:22:07,701
I never thought Mama Yaya and I
would see each other again.

370
00:22:10,287 --> 00:22:13,248
You two really clicked so quickly,
the two of you.

371
00:22:13,332 --> 00:22:14,458
I know, right?

372
00:22:14,541 --> 00:22:19,087
You know, it's like because
we've become such good friends,

373
00:22:19,171 --> 00:22:21,173
she feels like the sister I never had.

374
00:22:21,923 --> 00:22:23,717
You have a missing sister?

375
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:25,886
No, hello.

376
00:22:25,969 --> 00:22:27,179
It just feels that way.

377
00:22:27,804 --> 00:22:28,805
Yes.

378
00:22:29,306 --> 00:22:33,769
You know, I really hope
they allow your mom to come here.

379
00:22:33,852 --> 00:22:35,854
Then the three of us will be complete.

380
00:22:35,937 --> 00:22:39,900
Rosario, Rosenda, and Rosemarie.

381
00:22:41,485 --> 00:22:42,527
Who are they?

382
00:22:42,611 --> 00:22:44,780
Why, the three Claudines!

383
00:22:47,282 --> 00:22:49,493
Maybe you weren't even born back then!

384
00:22:49,576 --> 00:22:50,702
Wait a minute.

385
00:22:51,244 --> 00:22:52,788
What do you mean?

386
00:22:53,789 --> 00:22:55,999
We'll just be the <i>Powerpuff Girls</i>.
I'm Bubbles.

387
00:22:57,292 --> 00:23:00,587
Perfect. Mama Yaya and I
both love Blossom.

388
00:23:00,670 --> 00:23:04,341
Then Donabel can be Buttercup.

389
00:23:04,424 --> 00:23:06,176
She's the hothead, after all.

390
00:23:06,259 --> 00:23:07,385
Doesn't that fit?

391
00:23:08,804 --> 00:23:11,139
I hope they get approved.

392
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:12,265
Oh, dear.

393
00:23:12,349 --> 00:23:13,475
If that happens,

394
00:23:13,558 --> 00:23:15,143
poor Mario.

395
00:23:15,227 --> 00:23:17,854
We'll all be bossing him around
at the same time.

396
00:23:32,369 --> 00:23:35,455
Auntie Mercy, maybe we can get

397
00:23:35,539 --> 00:23:37,082
a future-husband discount here!

398
00:23:37,165 --> 00:23:37,999
There you go!

399
00:23:38,083 --> 00:23:40,836
A discount! Perfect timing.
I'm vlogging her!

400
00:23:40,919 --> 00:23:42,045
Come on.

401
00:23:43,755 --> 00:23:45,132
- Perfect timing. He's vlogging.
- You're something else, Mikoy.

402
00:23:45,215 --> 00:23:47,551
Fine, just add these two pieces.

403
00:23:47,634 --> 00:23:48,635
- Yes!
- Yes!

404
00:23:48,718 --> 00:23:49,803
Thank you, Mommy Mercy!

405
00:23:49,886 --> 00:23:50,971
Thank you!

406
00:23:51,054 --> 00:23:52,973
- There you go. Thank you!
- Thank you!

407
00:23:53,849 --> 00:23:55,517
You're really good at this, Mikoy!

408
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:56,852
Of course!

409
00:24:00,272 --> 00:24:01,690
Bro.

410
00:24:02,482 --> 00:24:03,483
Thank you.

411
00:24:05,652 --> 00:24:06,611
For what?

412
00:24:06,695 --> 00:24:07,821
For Mom.

413
00:24:08,905 --> 00:24:12,159
I didn't expect you guys
to accept her like that.

414
00:24:13,618 --> 00:24:14,953
Why wouldn't we?

415
00:24:15,036 --> 00:24:16,997
You're important to us.

416
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:19,207
So naturally, she's important to us too.

417
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:20,333
Really?

418
00:24:21,418 --> 00:24:22,919
Because, Bro,

419
00:24:23,003 --> 00:24:24,921
she just showed up out of nowhere,
and then

420
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:26,047
she's already the godmother.

421
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:29,843
I was surprised too.

422
00:24:29,926 --> 00:24:32,304
But look at her and Mom Tess, right?

423
00:24:32,387 --> 00:24:34,472
They act like
they've been friends forever!

424
00:24:35,140 --> 00:24:38,894
And it's actually nice
that she was Chiara's nanny.

425
00:24:39,728 --> 00:24:41,479
When you think about it,

426
00:24:42,063 --> 00:24:44,357
doesn't that mean you and Chiara
are practically siblings now?

427
00:24:44,441 --> 00:24:45,525
Right?

428
00:24:46,193 --> 00:24:47,152
Exactly.

429
00:24:47,235 --> 00:24:49,738
And Chiara seems happy about it, right?

430
00:24:50,864 --> 00:24:52,157
Of course!

431
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:53,992
Of course, and so am I.

432
00:24:54,576 --> 00:24:59,289
- I'm over the moon that my bride is happy.
- Nice.

433
00:25:01,166 --> 00:25:02,000
Hey!

434
00:25:02,083 --> 00:25:03,501
- Where are you from?
- I'm getting late.

435
00:25:03,585 --> 00:25:04,544
Where are you from?

436
00:25:04,628 --> 00:25:05,629
Not far.

437
00:25:05,712 --> 00:25:07,172
- All right.
- Just on the corner of the street.

438
00:25:07,255 --> 00:25:08,590
- Okay, buddy, head on in.
- Where is this located?

439
00:25:08,673 --> 00:25:10,383
Is this even Team Groom anymore?

440
00:25:10,926 --> 00:25:12,260
It's starting to look
like a security agency.

441
00:25:12,344 --> 00:25:13,553
Let me take a look first.

442
00:25:13,637 --> 00:25:15,305
- How do you know him?
- He's my brother.

443
00:25:15,388 --> 00:25:16,264
Okay, brother-in-law.

444
00:25:16,348 --> 00:25:17,599
- Sir.
- Bro.

445
00:25:17,682 --> 00:25:20,644
- I go here frequently.
- Could there be a reason for this?

446
00:25:21,603 --> 00:25:24,022
Wait, where are you heading? Stop.

447
00:25:24,105 --> 00:25:26,399
- What is that?
- Let me take a look.

448
00:25:26,483 --> 00:25:29,236
Don't they seem a little too serious?

449
00:25:29,319 --> 00:25:30,779
- Keep going straight.
- I need to hurry.

450
00:25:30,862 --> 00:25:33,281
Wait, Captain Pepe, Mario.

451
00:25:33,365 --> 00:25:34,574
What is this for?

452
00:25:34,658 --> 00:25:35,951
They weren't like this before.

453
00:25:54,803 --> 00:25:55,762
<i>I totally knew that.</i>

454
00:25:55,845 --> 00:25:58,848
<i>Those moves are full of doubts.</i>

455
00:25:58,932 --> 00:26:01,434
<i>I know, because I used to be like that!</i>

456
00:26:02,269 --> 00:26:04,104
Hang on. We have to take a selfie.

457
00:26:07,065 --> 00:26:09,484
We will make them jealous.
We're all so pretty today.

458
00:26:09,567 --> 00:26:11,194
See? I'm going to send this to him.

459
00:26:11,278 --> 00:26:13,405
Look, Tess sent a groupie.

460
00:26:14,906 --> 00:26:17,117
We can't lose. Mikoy!

461
00:26:21,037 --> 00:26:21,955
Carlota?

462
00:26:22,956 --> 00:26:24,207
What are you doing here?

463
00:26:24,291 --> 00:26:26,334
Did Senator Quintin send you?

464
00:26:26,418 --> 00:26:28,003
If he's the one who sent me,

465
00:26:28,086 --> 00:26:30,880
I wouldn't give you a tissue. Donabel,

466
00:26:32,090 --> 00:26:33,049
Let's go.
